  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which (-)-Duryne F interacts with the CD276 antigen, through a series of target-mediated pathways. The drug is implicated in targeting Caspase-5, which is subsequently targeted by multiple compounds, including Robinetinidol and Isotorachrysone-6-O-alpha-D-ribofuranoside. All these compounds are linked to the CD276 antigen, indicating a possible cascade of interactions where (-)-Duryne F may exert its effect via a shared target, Caspase-5, and ultimately influence the CD276 antigen. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a plausible pathway where (-)-Duryne F could act through Caspase-5 to modulate the CD276 antigen, though further experimental validation is required to confirm this hypothesis.",
